From: Gemini PDA Linux port <mratan/gemini-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: make the board dts validate

arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: make the board dts validate

Companion to the dtsi change.  Two of these are behavioural and are
called out where they happen:

  * hdmi_1v2 used "enable-gpios", which reg-fixed-voltage.c does not
    read -- it asks gpiolib for the nameless "gpio"/"gpios" property.
    GPIO247 has therefore never been driven by software and the rail has
    only ever been whatever the bootloader left it at.  Renamed, so the
    regulator now actually gates it.  First suspect if HDMI regresses.
  * The PMIC node is renamed mt6351 -> pmic, which is the child name
    mediatek,pwrap.yaml blesses.  The label is unchanged, so every &pmic
    reference still resolves.

The rest is inert: richtek,dvs-* demoted to a comment (fan53555.c reads
neither), a two-item compatible on the bq25896, SoC-specific compatibles
ahead of the generic tphy/mtu3 ones, and pinctrl groups renamed into the
schema's two-level shape.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -488,7 +488,7 @@
 	 * these defaults anyway; tuning is Phase 7.
 	 */
 	charger: charger@6b {
-		compatible = "ti,bq25896";
+		compatible = "ti,bq25896", "ti,bq25890";
 		reg = <0x6b>;
 		ti,charge-current = <2048000>;
 		ti,battery-regulation-voltage = <4208000>;
@@ -748,8 +748,11 @@
 		regulator-name = "vproc";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <600000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1393750>;
-		richtek,dvs-up-microvolt-per-usec = <32000>;
-		richtek,dvs-down-microvolt-per-usec = <4000>;
+		/*
+		 * Datasheet DVS ramp: 32 mV/us up, 4 mV/us down. Not expressed
+		 * as properties -- fan53555.c, which serves this compatible,
+		 * reads no such thing, so they were decoration.
+		 */
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
@@ -933,8 +936,8 @@
 	 * Vendor DTS: UART0 RX=GPIO97, TX=GPIO98.
 	 * These differ from the mainline uart0_pins_a (GPIO234/235).
